# Codex Host Overlay

- Resolve the active workspace in this order: explicit `-WorkspaceRoot` -> `DEV_HARNESS_WORKSPACE_ROOT` -> `WORKSPACE_ROOT` -> current directory inside an installed workspace.
- Read the resolved workspace's `AGENTS.md` first; it and the Harness runtime are authoritative, while user-level rules are defaults.
- Default language is Chinese. Use `.assistant\entry\task.ps1 status` for read-only v2 recovery; optional Memory requires an installed feature and explicit need or write authorization.
- Existing v1 tasks may use their compatibility runtime files; new v2 tasks use `.assistant/runtime`.
- Codex is a shared-pointer writer only when local entry rules identify it as entry host and the user explicitly continues or executes `mode=workflow`; inspect/status and standalone quick work never update pointers.
- Durable conclusions belong in maintained tracked artifacts; internal failed writes stay in `.assistant/runtime/failed-writes` and never enter a business inbox.
